  "format": "xitdb-script/1",
  "description": "An iterator on a sliced array list. It counts the elements it has given and not the slots it has passed, and a slice leaves the slots after the new end as they were. So a list with no unwritten elements stops where it should, and one with an unwritten element gives something past its end, which a read by index says isn't there. This pins what Zig does, and it looks like a mistake.",
